  "final_message": "The root cause was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`. Its filter was `status == \"open\" or (next_attempt_at is not None and next_attempt_at <= now)`. Because of the `or`, every open invoice counted as due on every billing cycle run, whatever the retry schedule said.\n\nI changed `or` to `and`. An invoice is now retried only when it is open, has a scheduled `next_attempt_at`, and that time has arrived. The tests (24) and mypy pass. I didn't add a test or run the specific scenario of 4 attempts in the first week, so the fix is confirmed by the existing suite only.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.",
